Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:40:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Booking requests: the answer window is five minutes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The window was one minute, which is shorter than it takes to walk to the phone
when you are holding clippers. The server now stamps a five-minute deadline; the
panel says so in its own words instead of repeating the old number.

One module (`src/utils/bookingWindow.js`) holds the number the panel PRINTS. The
deadline itself still comes from the server on every row (`expiresAt`), so the
panel never decides one — it counts down to the one it was given. The table's
"no answer in 60s" and the lifecycle's "no answer within 60 seconds" now read
"5 min", and the closed-window note reads "The 5-minute answer window has
closed".
